==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
A name given by {{w|Queen Victoria}} when it became a British colony in 1858, referring to the {{w|Columbia District}}, a territory drained by the [[Columbia River]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɹɪt.ɪʃ kəˈlʌm.bi.ə/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|En-ca-British Columbia.ogg|a=Canada}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{sid|en|Q1973}}{{place|en|province|in western|c/Canada|capital=Victoria|largest city=Vancouver}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1954|month=February|author=Trevor Holloway|title=Canada's Transcontinental Routes|journal=Railway Magazine|pages=127-128|text=In that year [1871] '''British Columbia''' decided to become part of the Dominion of Canada, on condition that a transcontinental railway should be completed without delay.}}

